        "title": "feat: add private AWS workspace service",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- add a private, SSM-only AWS workspace path that uses the AWS SDK default credential chain and fails closed on account, Region, ECS task-role identity, and permissions\n- enforce allowlisted small instance classes, encrypted configurable gp3 storage, private-subnet placement, no public address or SSH, IMDSv2, bounded networking, exact tags, lifecycle evidence, and idempotent cleanup\n- add a dedicated internal ALB/ECS/PostgreSQL coordinator stack with separate execution, task, and workspace roles\n- document the client URL/token contract, readiness checks, create/status/delete lifecycle, live canary, retirement procedure, and source-blind behavior contract\n\n## Why\n\nThe portable AWS path assumes static credentials and large default workspace resources. A dedicated-account deployment needs renewable task-role credentials, strict placement checks, smaller cost-bounded workspaces, and an isolated controller that does not depend on a reusable shared control plane.\n\n## Security and operating boundary\n\n- the dedicated deployment rejects static AWS access keys and requires the expected account, Region, ECS metadata, and task-role identity before provisioning\n- workspaces use a private subnet, no public IPv4/IPv6 address, no key pair or inbound security-group rules, IMDSv2, SSM bootstrap, encrypted gp3 volumes, and exact ownership tags\n- the stack fixes this deployment to on-demand capacity and exposes instance type and volume limits only through an explicit allowlist\n- this change contains no credentials, customer-specific identifiers, deployment actions, release changes, or version/tag changes\n- authenticated AWS lifecycle proof remains a separate pre-merge gate; this PR must stay unmerged until create, ready/status, logs/evidence, and idempotent delete are proven in the target account\n\n## Verification\n\nValidated at exact head `1f87ad7bd9cec728225d8d4045f09a8163a82a86`:\n\n- `go build -trimpath -o bin/crabbox ./cmd/crabbox`\n- `go vet ./...`\n- `go test -race ./...`\n- `scripts/test-go-modules.sh`\n- `scripts/check-go-coverage.sh 90.0`\n- `scripts/test-provider-lifecycles.sh`\n- `npm run format:check --prefix worker`\n- `npm run lint --prefix worker`\n- `npm run check --prefix worker`\n- `npm run check:node --prefix worker`\n- `npm test --prefix worker` (1,014 passed; 3 skipped)\n- `npm run build --prefix worker`\n- `npm run build:cloudflare-dynamic-workers --prefix worker`\n- `npm run build:node --prefix worker`\n- `node scripts/check-docker-base-images.mjs`\n- `node --test scripts/*.test.js`\n- `scripts/check-docs.sh`\n- `uvx cfn-lint deploy/aws/ecs-fargate-coordinator.yaml`\n- `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --self-test`\n- canonical structured autoreview: no accepted/actionable findings\n\n## Live acceptance still required\n\nFollow `docs/features/aws-private-workspaces.md` in an authenticated dedicated account to prove the fail-closed preflight, readiness endpoint, one create/status/delete canary, SSM and coordinator evidence, posture checks, and repeat-delete cleanup. No live cloud action is performed by this PR.",
